ComfyUI on openSUSE
==================

This package ships the ComfyUI tree read-only under /usr/share/comfyui
and the /usr/bin/comfyui launcher. Upstream's README assumes a git
checkout; here everything writable lives in a per-user profile, and
the server is started through the launcher.

Profile location
----------------

Unless overridden, the launcher uses $XDG_DATA_HOME/comfyui, falling
back to ~/.local/share/comfyui. It passes that directory to main.py
as --base-directory and points the asset database at
$base/user/comfyui.db via --database-url. Pass --base-directory or
--database-url explicitly to use somewhere else.

Where models go
---------------

Put checkpoints, LoRAs, VAEs and other assets under
$base/models/ (checkpoints in $base/models/checkpoints, created on
first start alongside $base/user). Point --extra-model-paths-config
at an extra_model_paths.yaml file to share model directories with
other installations.

CPU-only
--------

The openSUSE PyTorch build has neither CUDA nor ROCm support, so
ComfyUI runs on the CPU and falls back to it automatically. Expect
generation to be slow; this is a packaging limitation, not a bug.

Keep it on loopback
-------------------

The server listens on 127.0.0.1:8188 by default and has no login.
Keep it on loopback; passing --listen with a public address exposes
an unauthenticated API and web UI to the network.

Offline use
-----------

The browser UI otherwise contacts api.comfy.org and Hugging Face.
Start with --offline to stop that: it sets a restrictive
Content-Security-Policy header and disables partner nodes.
